Finn sees 11 tadpoles swimming in the pond.  Suddenly he sees 6 of them come out of hiding from under a lily pad, so now there are 11 + 6 = 17 tadpoles in the pond.  Then he sees 2 of them hide under a rock, so now there are 17 - 2 = 15 tadpoles in the pond.  Therefore, Finn can see 15 tadpoles in the pond now.

Final answer: \boxed{15}
