Watson works 10 hours a day, 5 days a week, so he works 10 * 5 = 50 hours a week. He earns $10 per hour, so he earns 50 * $10 = $500 per week. He also gets a $300 bonus each week if the company performs well. Since the company performed very well for the whole month, Watson earns $500 + $300 = $800 per week. There are 4 weeks in April, so Watson earns $800 * 4 = $3200 in April.

Final answer: \boxed{3200}
