Sandy needs 4 weeks to lose the same amount of weight that Joey loses in a single week. If Joey loses 8 pounds in 4 weeks, then Sandy will lose 8 pounds in 4 weeks. Therefore, it will take Sandy 4 weeks to lose the same amount of weight that Joey loses in a single week.

Final answer: \boxed{4}
#### 4

Oscar starts with 24 lollipops. He eats 2 on his way to school, so he has 24 - 2 = 22 lollipops left. He then passes 14 out to his friends, so he has 22 - 14 = 8 lollipops left. He buys twice as many lollipops on his way home as he gave to his friends, so he buys 2 * 14 = 28 lollipops. He now has 8 + 28 = 36 lollipops. He eats 3 more that night, so he has 36 - 3 = 33 lollipops left. He eats 2 more in the morning, so he has 33 - 2 = 31 lollipops left. Therefore, Oscar has 31 lollipops.

Final answer: \boxed{31}
#### 31

Mason needs 30 ounces of sugar to make a batch of suckers and 70 ounces of sugar to make a batch of fudge. To make 8 batches of suckers, he needs 8 * 30 = 240 ounces of sugar. To make 1 batch of fudge, he needs 70 ounces of sugar. Therefore, the total amount of sugar he needs is 240 + 70 = 310 ounces.

Final answer: \boxed{310}
