Mrs. Sherman made a dozen bread rolls for breakfast, which means she made 12 bread rolls. After feeding her 6 children with one each, she has 12 - 6 = 6 bread rolls left. She then broke each of the remaining rolls into 8 pieces, so she has 6 * 8 = 48 pieces of rolls. Therefore, she fed 48 pieces of rolls to the chickens.

Final answer: \boxed{48}
